      "id": 1,
      "text": "St. Florian sprang up in the 1870s when German settlers bought the land and named the town after Saint Florian, the patron saint of firefighters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Florian%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in St. Florian in 1879 and closed in 1904, marking the town’s early communication link.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Florian%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "St. Florian officially incorporated in 1970, becoming a recognized municipality within Lauderdale County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/st-florian/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nestled in northwestern Alabama’s Lauderdale County, St. Florian is part of the Florence‑Muscle Shoals metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
